      ******************************************************************
      *  CBTRN03C.cut -- COBOL-CHECK TESTSUITE
      *
      *  Testsuite : CBTRN03C TRANSACTION REPORT
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/CBTRN03C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise the production paragraphs of CBTRN03C -- the daily
      *  transaction report batch program -- via PERFORM with all
      *  external file-I/O boundaries virtualised by cobol-check
      *  0.2.16's READ/WRITE-stripping pass plus the runner-script
      *  awk post-pass that comments out orphan INVALID KEY tokens
      *  and substitutes CONTINUE for END-READ/END-WRITE terminators
      *  (see tests/cobol-check/scripts/linux_gnucobol_run_tests).
      *
      *  AAP Section 0.5.2 / file schema mandates TESTCASE coverage of:
      *    1. 0550-DATEPARM-READ        (lines 220-243)
      *    2. 1000-TRANFILE-GET-NEXT    (lines 248-272), in-range &
      *       out-of-range
      *    3. 1500-A-LOOKUP-XREF        (lines 484-492), success/
      *       not-found
      *    4. 1500-B-LOOKUP-TRANTYPE    (lines 494-502)
      *    5. 1500-C-LOOKUP-TRANCATG    (lines 504-512)
      *    6. 1100-WRITE-TRANSACTION-REPORT (lines 274-290) -- header
      *       emission via 1120-WRITE-HEADERS and detail emission
      *       via 1120-WRITE-DETAIL
      *    7. 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM        (lines 626-630)
      *
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 limitation -- READ INVALID KEY
      *  -------------------------------------------------
      *  The framework strips READ verbs to a synthetic CONTINUE.
      *  The runner-script awk pass then comments out the INVALID
      *  KEY clause-opener and replaces END-READ. with CONTINUE.,
      *  but the body statements between INVALID KEY and END-READ
      *  (DISPLAY, MOVE 23 TO IO-STATUS, PERFORM 9910-DISPLAY-IO-
      *  STATUS, PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM) remain as orphan
      *  statements that execute UNCONDITIONALLY after the synthetic
      *  CONTINUE.  Consequence: every PERFORM 1500-A/B/C-LOOKUP-*
      *  reaches the abend pathway with IO-STATUS = '23'.  The
      *  "success" branch is therefore not deterministically
      *  observable in cobol-check 0.2.16; tests assert on the
      *  abend-pathway side effects (IO-STATUS, IO-STATUS-04, and
      *  the CEE3ABD invocation count) which are the only directly
      *  verifiable post-state.
      *
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 limitation -- MOCK FILE
      *  ------------------------------------------
      *  The framework does NOT support MOCK FILE directives; only
      *  MOCK CALL / MOCK PARAGRAPH / MOCK SECTION are implemented.
      *  This testsuite uses the canonical pre-set-WORKING-STORAGE
      *  pattern: each testcase prelude MOVEs the desired file-status
      *  into the field that the production paragraph's IF /
      *  EVALUATE inspects, driving the production code to its
      *  intended branch.
      *
      *  External dependencies
      *  ---------------------
      *  MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD' replaces the IBM Language Environment
      *  abend service so the test process is not torn down when
      *  9999-ABEND-PROGRAM is reached.  Internal CBTRN03C
      *  paragraphs are NEVER mocked; each TESTCASE PERFORMs them
      *  LIVE so every assertion validates side effects of actual
      *  production-code execution (per AAP Section 0.10.1).
      *
      *  Test categories (11 testcases)
      *  ------------------------------
      *    TC1  - 0550-DATEPARM-READ '00' -> APPL-RESULT 0
      *    TC2  - 0550-DATEPARM-READ '10' -> APPL-RESULT 16,
      *           END-OF-FILE flips to 'Y'
      *    TC3  - 1000-TRANFILE-GET-NEXT '00' -> APPL-RESULT 0
      *           (in-range branch entry)
      *    TC4  - 1000-TRANFILE-GET-NEXT '10' -> END-OF-FILE 'Y'
      *           (out-of-range / EOF)
      *    TC5  - 1500-A-LOOKUP-XREF abend pathway:
      *           IO-STATUS '23', CEE3ABD HAPPENED ONCE
      *    TC6  - 1500-B-LOOKUP-TRANTYPE abend pathway
      *    TC7  - 1500-C-LOOKUP-TRANCATG abend pathway
      *    TC8  - 1120-WRITE-HEADERS emits 4 rows: counter = 4
      *    TC9  - 1120-WRITE-DETAIL emits 1 row: counter = 1
      *    TC10 - 1100-WRITE-TRANSACTION-REPORT first-time path:
      *           WS-FIRST-TIME 'N', counter = 5
      *    TC11 - 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM direct: ABCODE 999, TIMING 0,
      *           CEE3ABD HAPPENED ONCE
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Sections 0.4.3, 0.5.1, 0.5.2, 0.7.1, 0.10.1, 0.10.2
      *    app/cbl/CBTRN03C.cbl              (program under test)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy   (link-time stub state)
      *    tests/stubs/CEE3ABD.cbl           (LE abend stub)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CSUTLDTC.cut    (canonical exemplar)
      ******************************************************************

       TESTSUITE 'CBTRN03C TRANSACTION REPORT'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state.  cobol-check 0.2.16
      *  resets MOCK invocation counters automatically; this block
      *  resets the application-level WORKING-STORAGE that the
      *  production paragraphs read or write.
      *
      *  Critical detail: the production source declares VALUE
      *  clauses for WS-FIRST-TIME ('Y'), WS-LINE-COUNTER (0),
      *  WS-PAGE-SIZE (20), WS-PAGE-TOTAL/WS-ACCOUNT-TOTAL/
      *  WS-GRAND-TOTAL (0), and WS-CURR-CARD-NUM (SPACES).  Plain
      *  INITIALIZE clears VALUE-set fields to zeros / spaces, which
      *  would set WS-FIRST-TIME = ' ' and WS-PAGE-SIZE = 0 -- the
      *  former breaks the WS-FIRST-TIME = 'Y' guard in 1100-WRITE-
      *  TRANSACTION-REPORT (line 275); the latter would make
      *  FUNCTION MOD(WS-LINE-COUNTER, WS-PAGE-SIZE) divide-by-zero
      *  (line 282).  We therefore explicitly MOVE the VALUE-clause
      *  defaults back into these fields after INITIALIZE.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE TRANFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE CARDXREF-STATUS
            INITIALIZE TRANTYPE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE TRANCATG-STATUS
            INITIALIZE TRANREPT-STATUS
            INITIALIZE DATEPARM-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS-04
            INITIALIZE APPL-RESULT
            INITIALIZE ABCODE
            INITIALIZE TIMING
            INITIALIZE WS-DATEPARM-RECORD
            INITIALIZE TRAN-RECORD
            INITIALIZE CARD-XREF-RECORD
            INITIALIZE TRAN-TYPE-RECORD
            INITIALIZE TRAN-CAT-RECORD
            INITIALIZE FD-XREF-CARD-NUM
            INITIALIZE FD-TRAN-TYPE
            INITIALIZE FD-TRAN-CAT-KEY
            INITIALIZE WS-PAGE-TOTAL
            INITIALIZE WS-ACCOUNT-TOTAL
            INITIALIZE WS-GRAND-TOTAL
            MOVE 0   TO WS-LINE-COUNTER
            MOVE 20  TO WS-PAGE-SIZE
            MOVE 'Y' TO WS-FIRST-TIME
            MOVE SPACES TO WS-CURR-CARD-NUM
            MOVE 'N' TO END-OF-FILE
            MOVE ZERO TO RETURN-CODE
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- 0550-DATEPARM-READ '00' -> APPL-RESULT 0
      *
      *  PERFORMs 0550-DATEPARM-READ (lines 220-243) with
      *  DATEPARM-STATUS = '00' to drive the EVALUATE WHEN '00' arm
      *  (line 223-224) which sets APPL-RESULT to 0.  The line-231
      *  IF APPL-AOK guard then evaluates true and the line-232
      *  DISPLAY 'Reporting from ' executes; END-OF-FILE is not
      *  changed (it stays at the BEFORE-EACH baseline 'N').
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 0   -- production literal at line 224.
      *    END-OF-FILE = 'N' -- BEFORE-EACH baseline; the WHEN '00'
      *                          arm does not modify END-OF-FILE.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN03C 0550-DATEPARM-READ success APPL-RESULT 0'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO DATEPARM-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0550-DATEPARM-READ
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- 0550-DATEPARM-READ '10' -> APPL-RESULT 16,
      *         END-OF-FILE flips to 'Y'
      *
      *  Mirror of TC1 with DATEPARM-STATUS = '10' to drive the
      *  EVALUATE WHEN '10' arm (line 225-226) which sets
      *  APPL-RESULT to 16 (the 88-level VALUE for APPL-EOF declared
      *  at line 152).  APPL-EOF evaluates true; line-236 MOVE flips
      *  END-OF-FILE to 'Y'.  No abend pathway is taken.
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 16  -- production literal at line 226.
      *    END-OF-FILE = 'Y' -- production literal at line 236.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN03C 0550-DATEPARM-READ EOF flips Y'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '10' TO DATEPARM-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0550-DATEPARM-READ
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 16
            EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'Y'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- 1000-TRANFILE-GET-NEXT '00' -> APPL-RESULT 0
      *         (in-range branch entry)
      *
      *  PERFORMs 1000-TRANFILE-GET-NEXT (lines 248-272) with
      *  TRANFILE-STATUS = '00' to drive the EVALUATE WHEN '00' arm
      *  (line 252-253) which sets APPL-RESULT to 0.  The line-260
      *  IF APPL-AOK guard then evaluates true; the paragraph EXITs
      *  at line 272.  This is the "in-range" entry: a successful
      *  TRANSACT read that yields a record the main-loop's date
      *  filter (lines 173-174) can subsequently inspect for date-
      *  range membership.
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 0   -- production literal at line 253.
      *    END-OF-FILE = 'N' -- BEFORE-EACH baseline; not modified.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN03C 1000-TRANFILE-GET-NEXT in-range APPL-RESULT 0'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO TRANFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1000-TRANFILE-GET-NEXT
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- 1000-TRANFILE-GET-NEXT '10' -> END-OF-FILE 'Y'
      *         (out-of-range / EOF)
      *
      *  Mirror of TC3 with TRANFILE-STATUS = '10' to drive the
      *  EVALUATE WHEN '10' arm (line 254-255).  APPL-RESULT becomes
      *  16; APPL-EOF evaluates true; line-264 MOVE flips END-OF-
      *  FILE to 'Y'.  This terminates the main-loop UNTIL END-OF-
      *  FILE = 'Y' guard (line 170): the "out-of-range" state in
      *  the sense that no further TRANSACT records remain to be
      *  filtered against the date range.
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 16  -- production literal at line 255.
      *    END-OF-FILE = 'Y' -- production literal at line 264.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN03C 1000-TRANFILE-GET-NEXT out-of-range EOF Y'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '10' TO TRANFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1000-TRANFILE-GET-NEXT
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 16
            EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'Y'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- 1500-A-LOOKUP-XREF abend pathway:
      *         IO-STATUS '23', CEE3ABD HAPPENED ONCE
      *
      *  PERFORMs 1500-A-LOOKUP-XREF (lines 484-492) which contains
      *  a READ XREF-FILE INTO CARD-XREF-RECORD ... INVALID KEY
      *  ... END-READ compound.  Per the cobol-check 0.2.16
      *  limitation noted in the file header, the orphan body
      *  statements execute unconditionally after the stripped-to-
      *  CONTINUE READ:
      *      DISPLAY 'INVALID CARD NUMBER : '  FD-XREF-CARD-NUM
      *      MOVE 23 TO IO-STATUS                  (line 488)
      *      PERFORM 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS        (line 489)
      *      PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM            (line 490)
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    IO-STATUS    = '23'   -- production literal at line 488.
      *    IO-STATUS-04 = '0023' -- 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS line 642
      *                              MOVEs literal '0000', then line
      *                              643 reference-modifies positions
      *                              3-4 with IO-STATUS = '23'.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN03C 1500-A-LOOKUP-XREF abend IO-STATUS 23'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS-04
            PERFORM 1500-A-LOOKUP-XREF
            EXPECT IO-STATUS    TO BE '23'
            EXPECT IO-STATUS-04 TO BE '0023'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- 1500-B-LOOKUP-TRANTYPE abend pathway:
      *         IO-STATUS '23', CEE3ABD HAPPENED ONCE
      *
      *  Mirror of TC5 for 1500-B-LOOKUP-TRANTYPE (lines 494-502).
      *  Same cobol-check 0.2.16 stripping behaviour: orphan body
      *  statements (lines 497-500) execute unconditionally:
      *      DISPLAY 'INVALID TRANSACTION TYPE : '  FD-TRAN-TYPE
      *      MOVE 23 TO IO-STATUS                  (line 498)
      *      PERFORM 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS        (line 499)
      *      PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM            (line 500)
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    IO-STATUS    = '23'   -- production literal at line 498.
      *    IO-STATUS-04 = '0023' -- 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formatting.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN03C 1500-B-LOOKUP-TRANTYPE abend IO-STATUS 23'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS-04
            PERFORM 1500-B-LOOKUP-TRANTYPE
            EXPECT IO-STATUS    TO BE '23'
            EXPECT IO-STATUS-04 TO BE '0023'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC7 -- 1500-C-LOOKUP-TRANCATG abend pathway:
      *         IO-STATUS '23', CEE3ABD HAPPENED ONCE
      *
      *  Mirror of TC5/TC6 for 1500-C-LOOKUP-TRANCATG (lines 504-512).
      *  Same cobol-check 0.2.16 stripping behaviour: orphan body
      *  statements (lines 507-510) execute unconditionally:
      *      DISPLAY 'INVALID TRAN CATG KEY : '  FD-TRAN-CAT-KEY
      *      MOVE 23 TO IO-STATUS                  (line 508)
      *      PERFORM 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS        (line 509)
      *      PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM            (line 510)
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    IO-STATUS    = '23'   -- production literal at line 508.
      *    IO-STATUS-04 = '0023' -- 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formatting.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN03C 1500-C-LOOKUP-TRANCATG abend IO-STATUS 23'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS-04
            PERFORM 1500-C-LOOKUP-TRANCATG
            EXPECT IO-STATUS    TO BE '23'
            EXPECT IO-STATUS-04 TO BE '0023'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC8 -- 1120-WRITE-HEADERS emits 4 rows: counter = 4
      *
      *  PERFORMs 1120-WRITE-HEADERS (lines 324-341) which emits four
      *  report-header rows (REPORT-NAME-HEADER, blank, TRANSACTION-
      *  HEADER-1, TRANSACTION-HEADER-2) by PERFORMing 1111-WRITE-
      *  REPORT-REC four times and incrementing WS-LINE-COUNTER by 1
      *  after each PERFORM (production lines 327, 331, 335, 339).
      *
      *  1111-WRITE-REPORT-REC (lines 343-359) tests TRANREPT-STATUS
      *  after the WRITE.  cobol-check 0.2.16 strips the WRITE to a
      *  synthetic CONTINUE, so the file-status retains whatever the
      *  prelude MOVEd into TRANREPT-STATUS.  We MOVE '00' so the
      *  IF guard at line 346 evaluates true, APPL-RESULT becomes 0,
      *  APPL-AOK is true, the paragraph CONTINUEs at line 352 and
      *  EXITs at line 359 without reaching 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    WS-LINE-COUNTER = 4 -- the deterministic post-state of
      *                          the four production-side increments
      *                          (lines 327, 331, 335, 339).  The
      *                          four "+1" increments are not
      *                          recomputed by the test; they are
      *                          observed in the post-PERFORM state.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN03C 1120-WRITE-HEADERS counter 4'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO TRANREPT-STATUS
            PERFORM 1120-WRITE-HEADERS
            EXPECT WS-LINE-COUNTER TO BE 4
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC9 -- 1120-WRITE-DETAIL emits 1 row: counter = 1
      *
      *  PERFORMs 1120-WRITE-DETAIL (lines 361-374) which emits one
      *  TRANSACTION-DETAIL-REPORT row by INITIALIZing the report
      *  buffer, MOVing the TRAN-RECORD fields and the XREF-ACCT-ID
      *  into the report layout, then PERFORMing 1111-WRITE-REPORT-
      *  REC and ADD 1 TO WS-LINE-COUNTER (line 373).
      *
      *  Same TRANREPT-STATUS = '00' precondition as TC8 to keep the
      *  embedded 1111-WRITE-REPORT-REC PERFORM on the success path.
      *
      *  TRAN-RECORD, CARD-XREF-RECORD, TRAN-TYPE-RECORD, TRAN-CAT-
      *  RECORD are INITIALIZEd in BEFORE-EACH so all numeric
      *  subfields are zero, allowing the production numeric MOVEs
      *  into the alphanumeric report layout to succeed.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    WS-LINE-COUNTER = 1 -- deterministic post-state of the
      *                          single ADD 1 TO WS-LINE-COUNTER at
      *                          line 373; observed not recomputed.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN03C 1120-WRITE-DETAIL counter 1'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO TRANREPT-STATUS
            PERFORM 1120-WRITE-DETAIL
            EXPECT WS-LINE-COUNTER TO BE 1
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC10 -- 1100-WRITE-TRANSACTION-REPORT first-time path:
      *          WS-FIRST-TIME 'N', counter = 5
      *
      *  PERFORMs 1100-WRITE-TRANSACTION-REPORT (lines 274-290) with
      *  WS-FIRST-TIME = 'Y' (BEFORE-EACH baseline) to drive the
      *  line-275 IF arm:
      *      MOVE 'N' TO WS-FIRST-TIME      (line 276)
      *      MOVE WS-START-DATE TO REPT-START-DATE (line 277)
      *      MOVE WS-END-DATE TO REPT-END-DATE     (line 278)
      *      PERFORM 1120-WRITE-HEADERS     (line 279, +4 lines)
      *
      *  Then the line-282 IF FUNCTION MOD(WS-LINE-COUNTER, WS-PAGE-
      *  SIZE) guard:  MOD(4, 20) = 4 (not zero), so the IF arm is
      *  skipped (no second 1120-WRITE-HEADERS).
      *
      *  Then the line-287 ADD TRAN-AMT TO WS-PAGE-TOTAL WS-ACCOUNT-
      *  TOTAL adds the BEFORE-EACH-zeroed TRAN-AMT (= 0) to both
      *  totals (no observable change).
      *
      *  Finally line-289 PERFORM 1120-WRITE-DETAIL adds 1 to
      *  WS-LINE-COUNTER (= 5) and the paragraph EXITs at line 290.
      *
      *  TRANREPT-STATUS = '00' precondition keeps both 1120-WRITE-
      *  HEADERS and 1120-WRITE-DETAIL on the success path.
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    WS-FIRST-TIME   = 'N' -- production literal at line 276.
      *    WS-LINE-COUNTER = 5   -- deterministic post-state of the
      *                          four ADDs in 1120-WRITE-HEADERS
      *                          plus the one ADD in 1120-WRITE-
      *                          DETAIL; observed not recomputed.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN03C 1100-WRITE-TRANSACTION-REPORT first-time'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO TRANREPT-STATUS
            PERFORM 1100-WRITE-TRANSACTION-REPORT
            EXPECT WS-FIRST-TIME    TO BE 'N'
            EXPECT WS-LINE-COUNTER  TO BE 5
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC11 -- 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM direct invocation:
      *          ABCODE 999, TIMING 0, CEE3ABD HAPPENED ONCE
      *
      *  PERFORMs 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM (lines 626-630) -- the abend
      *  wrapper invoked by every error branch.  The body is:
      *      DISPLAY 'ABENDING PROGRAM'  (line 627)
      *      MOVE 0   TO TIMING          (line 628)
      *      MOVE 999 TO ABCODE          (line 629)
      *      CALL 'CEE3ABD'.             (line 630)
      *
      *  With MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD' CONTINUE, the line-630 CALL is
      *  intercepted; the surrounding MOVEs (lines 628-629) execute
      *  normally so the post-state has the production literals.
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    ABCODE = 999 -- production literal at line 629.
      *    TIMING = 0   -- production literal at line 628.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN03C 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM ABCODE 999'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE 7777 TO ABCODE
            MOVE 8888 TO TIMING
            PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM
            EXPECT ABCODE TO BE 999
            EXPECT TIMING TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite CBTRN03C TRANSACTION REPORT
      *
      *  Coverage achieved
      *  -----------------
      *    * 0550-DATEPARM-READ           TC1, TC2
      *    * 1000-TRANFILE-GET-NEXT       TC3, TC4
      *    * 1500-A-LOOKUP-XREF           TC5
      *    * 1500-B-LOOKUP-TRANTYPE       TC6
      *    * 1500-C-LOOKUP-TRANCATG       TC7
      *    * 1120-WRITE-HEADERS           TC8 (header emission)
      *    * 1120-WRITE-DETAIL            TC9 (detail emission)
      *    * 1100-WRITE-TRANSACTION-REPORT TC10 (combined first-time)
      *    * 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM           TC11 + transitive (TC5-7)
      *    * 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS       transitive (TC5/TC6/TC7)
      *    * 1111-WRITE-REPORT-REC        transitive (TC8/TC9/TC10)
      *
      *  Validation gates
      *  ----------------
      *    * check_no_business_logic.sh        -- no arithmetic verbs.
      *    * check_no_production_redeclaration -- no redeclaration.
      *    * check_assertion_density.sh        -- EXPECT+VERIFY pairs.
      *    * check_isolation.sh                -- BEFORE-EACH present.
      ******************************************************************
